course: dictionary
lesson: 16132
title: Whiteness: the look of white
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Whiteness is a noun. It names the quality of being white, like snow, milk or a clean page. When you meet it, ask yourself what is white. The words around it will tell you.
explain: «The whiteness of the snow hid the path.» Snow is white, so whiteness here means the white quality of the snow. You cannot touch whiteness, but you can see it, and it describes how something looks.
explain: Whiteness can also describe skin. «Her face had a strange whiteness after the fright.» Here whiteness means paleness: her skin had lost its usual colour because she was scared. The same word can mean pure white or paleness, so check the clues.
explain: Ask: is the sentence about snow, milk, light or a clean page? Then whiteness means the quality of being white. Is it about a face, after illness or fright? Then whiteness means paleness of the skin.
fact: Whiteness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «the whiteness», not «a whiteness».
fact: «Whiteness» means the quality of being white, like snow, milk or a clean page.
fact: «Whiteness» can also mean paleness of the skin, for example from being ill or frightened.
fact: In science, white light contains all the colours of the rainbow.
fact: «Dazzling whiteness» means white so bright that it makes your eyes squint.
exercise: «The whiteness of the snow hid the path.» What does whiteness mean here? | Coldness | * The quality of being white | Softness | Thickness
exercise: «Her face had a strange whiteness after the fright.» What does whiteness describe? | Wet hair | A dark bruise | A loud noise | * Paleness of the skin
exercise: In science, what does white light contain? | Only yellow light | Just black dots | Nothing at all | * All the colours of the rainbow
test: «The dazzling whiteness of the new sheets made Sam squint.» What does dazzling whiteness mean? | Dark and grey | * Blindingly bright white | Sticky and wet | Soft and warm
test: «Mum said the whiteness of the milk looked fresh.» What does whiteness refer to in this sentence? | The taste of the milk | Sadness in the kitchen | * The white colour and quality of the milk | Paleness of a person's face
exam: «After the fright, the whiteness of his face worried his mum.» What does whiteness mean in this sentence? | A loud noise in the street | Heavy snow falling all night | A bright red colour | * Paleness of the skin, because he had been frightened
